The class `Functions` consists mainly of lightweight factory methods and simple functional adapters (e.g., identity, empty consumers, small wrappers around existing functional interfaces). These operations are trivial, have negligible computational cost, and are not algorithmically complex. Benchmarking such micro‑operations with JMH would not provide meaningful performance insights and would mostly measure JVM overhead rather than the logic itself. Therefore, generating JMH benchmarks for this code is unnecessary.